direct-nested-def
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: lift "a Direct mark inside a nested definition" for the one shape
  that a direct block needs and cannot express today: a PARAMETERLESS
  local `def` at the block's program type whose body carries marks —
  `def plan = effect(GetPlan(user.planId))` beside a `lazy val user`.
  Its body is its own program, so compile it through `pipeline` (as a
  try body already is) under a fresh symbol at the widened program
  type, and rewrite its uses: a coloured use becomes a mark (a bind per
  use = by name), a bare use the program itself. Defs with parameters
  and non-program defs keep the refusal.
files: src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/test/scala/TestDirectOnce.scala,
  docs/direct-style.md, specs/direct-macro.md, CHANGELOG.md
